{
  "id": "COMPOUND:9315 - PROTEIN:473",
  "verbalization": "Clove oil is implicated in the activation of G-protein coupled estrogen receptor 1, which is a key target for multiple compounds, including Fibrauretinoside A and 5-Hydroxy-2-[2-(2-Hydroxyphenyl)Ethyl]Chromone. These compounds, in turn, target Diacylglycerol kinase gamma, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Clove oil may influence this enzyme. The evidence is supported by multiple paths, all of which link Clove oil to Diacylglycerol kinase gamma through a common intermediate, G-protein coupled estrogen receptor 1. The final scores indicate a consistent and plausible relationship, though the exact mode of action remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple compounds targeting the same receptor and enzyme supports a mechanistic link, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the biological relevance of this interaction.",
